@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium use case diagram — e-commerce with three actors, eight use cases, «include», «extend», and actor generalization.
'   usecase:      Teach «include» (mandatory delegation), «extend» (optional, condition-gated extension), and actor generalization.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       E-Commerce
' ============================================================================
title Example Use Case Diagram - Medium E-Commerce

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Actors:  Customer, Guest (not yet logged in), Admin.
# Use cases: Browse Catalog, Search, Add to Cart, Checkout, Pay,
#            Apply Discount, Ship Order, Manage Products.
# Relationships:
#   - «include»  : Checkout MANDATORILY invokes Pay (every checkout pays).
#   - «extend»   : Apply Discount OPTIONALLY extends Checkout (only if a code
#                  is entered) — condition shown in a note.
#   - actor generalization: Guest --|> Customer (a Guest is a kind of Customer
#                  who can browse but cannot checkout until authenticated).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

left to right direction

actor "Customer" as cust
actor "Guest"    as guest
actor "Admin"    as admin

' ACTOR GENERALIZATION: Guest is-a Customer (inherits all Customer use cases).
guest --|> cust

rectangle "Online Store" {
  usecase "Browse Catalog"   as ucBrowse
  usecase "Search Products"  as ucSearch
  usecase "Add to Cart"      as ucAdd
  usecase "Checkout"         as ucCheckout
  usecase "Pay"              as ucPay
  usecase "Apply Discount"   as ucDiscount
  usecase "Ship Order"       as ucShip
  usecase "Manage Products"  as ucManage
}

' --- Associations -------------------------------------------------------
cust  --> ucBrowse
cust  --> ucSearch
cust  --> ucAdd
cust  --> ucCheckout
admin --> ucManage
admin --> ucShip

' --- «include»: Checkout always invokes Pay (mandatory) ----------------
ucCheckout .> ucPay : <<include>>

' --- «extend»: Apply Discount optionally extends Checkout ---------------
' Dashed arrow points FROM the extending use case TO the base use case.
ucDiscount .> ucCheckout : <<extend>>

note right of ucDiscount
  <b>«extend» — optional</b>
  Apply Discount extends Checkout.
  Condition: { discount code entered }.
  The base use case is complete WITHOUT
  the extension; the extension ADDS
  behaviour only when the condition holds.
end note

note bottom of ucPay
  <b>«include» — mandatory</b>
  Checkout includes Pay.  Pay ALWAYS
  executes as part of Checkout — there is
  no condition.  Use «include» to factor
  out common, required behaviour that
  several base use cases share.
end note

@enduml
